advanced disease, excluding adjuvant or sarcoma trials) and 12 were excluded.

### 2. Task outcome (extremely detailed version):
Each study was evaluated against the selection criteria: must be a randomized controlled trial (RCT) comparing a 
chemotherapy regimen with another intervention (which may be a different chemotherapy or non‑chemotherapy) in patients 
with advanced disease; studies focused on adjuvant therapy or sarcomatous tumours were to be excluded. Using the titles 
and abstracts provided, I assessed study design, intervention comparators, disease stage, and any exclusionary cues. 
When uncertainty remained, I applied the conservative rule to include the study. The detailed decisions are listed 
below.

### 3. Additional context (if relevant):
All judgments were based solely on the information supplied in the titles and abstracts; no full‑text review was 
performed. The conservative approach means that borderline cases (e.g., studies lacking explicit randomization language 
but implying comparative treatment) were included to avoid missing potentially eligible evidence. No studies were 
excluded solely on the basis of vague terminology without a clear contraindication (adjuvant or sarcoma focus). The 
final tally reflects a balanced application of the criteria.

