│ or metastatic endometrial adenocarcinoma.", "background": "Although endometrial adenocarcinoma is a common           │
│ gynaecological cancer, a comparatively small proportion of patients present with, or develop, recurrent or advanced  │
│ disease. However, for those women whose disease does progress or recur the prognosis is poor and the best treatment  │
│ is yet to be identified. Co‐morbidity, including obesity and cardiac disease, and concerns over toxicity have        │
│ prevented more extensive studies of cytotoxic chemotherapy, although there are a number of active agents.",          │
